  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric stack on CaF2 substrate for dual-band infrared transmission. Layer sequence: Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS|Ge|ZnS (22 finite layers). Initialize all layer thicknesses with random uniform distribution centered at 220 nm with ±40% variance (range approximately 132-308 nm initial). Set optimization bounds to [20, 450] nm for all 22 thickness variables. Disable adaptive step-scaling for first 50% of optimization budget. Use coherent transfer matrix solver at normal incidence. Wavelength range 2500-5000 nm. Four mean-transmittance objectives: maximize in 3250-3350 nm (methane band), maximize in 4200-4300 nm (CO2 band), minimize in 2500-3100 nm (blocking), minimize in 4450-5000 nm (blocking). Run both gradient_thickness and differential_evolution_thickness optimizers. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 22-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric stack on a CaF2 substrate for dual-band infrared transmission at normal incidence. Maximize mean transmittance in 3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm, while minimizing mean transmittance in 2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm. Initialize thicknesses near 220 nm with optimization bounds restricted to 20-450 nm. Use a coherent smatrix solver and evaluate against fixed manufacturing and material constraints.",
